specs/hal-engine-websocket-protocol/spec.md:682:- An entry still streaming when its conversation is resumed is replayed with `isStreaming: false` and `truncated: true`: the rest of its turn streams to the connection that started it, so this one would wait for a commit that never comes ([validated by: replays an entry whose turn is still running as finished and truncated, leaving the stored entry as it is](../../src/transport/sessionResume.test.ts#L364)).
specs/hal-engine-websocket-protocol/spec.md:683:- With the server's `latest` option, a client that has lost the id, after a page refresh for instance, MAY connect without one and still rejoin its user's most recent conversation, and sends `?new=1` to start a new conversation instead ([validated by: with latest on, rejoins the most recently active session of a user whose connect names none](../../src/transport/sessionResume.test.ts#L428), [validated by: with latest on, starts a new session for a user with none, and on ?new=1 even when one exists](../../src/transport/sessionResume.test.ts#L445)).
specs/hal-engine-conversation-list/spec.md:74:- A client sends `{type: 'list_sessions', limit?, before?}` and receives `{type: 'session_list', sessions}` for the socket's authenticated user, with `createdAt` and `updatedAt` serialised as ISO-8601 strings and any client-supplied `userId` ignored ([validated by: answers list_sessions for the authenticated user with ISO dates, forwarding limit and before while ignoring any client userId](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L93); [validated by: lists sessions for the authenticated user, ignoring a userId in the frame](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L91)).
specs/hal-engine-conversation-list/spec.md:75:- A store without `listFor` answers `{type: 'session_list', sessions: []}`, and a throwing `listFor` logs an error on the `ws` category and answers `{type: 'error', code: 'SERVER_ERROR'}` ([validated by: answers an empty session_list when the store has no listFor, and SERVER_ERROR with a ws error log when listFor throws](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L134)).
specs/hal-engine-conversation-list/spec.md:76:- The validator accepts an optional non-negative integer `limit` and an optional `before` cursor whose `sessionId` is 1–128 characters and whose `updatedAt` parses as a valid timestamp, rejecting any other `list_sessions` payload with `INVALID_MESSAGE` without calling `listFor` ([validated by: accepts a list_sessions cursor and rejects malformed list pagination fields](../../src/transport/ws/validation.test.ts#L24); [validated by: accepts a bare list_sessions frame and rejects a malformed limit or before with INVALID_MESSAGE without calling listFor](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L154)).
